sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg within-feather Turing wavelength of Anas platyrhynchos at 378.4 µm (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 76.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 integrates the Schnakenberg Jacobian (trace -0.200, det +1) with cubic saturation on a periodic vane. k_c = 0.623 and k_star = 0.524 rad/cell after Du is scaled so lambda_star = 378.34 µm (anchor 378.4 µm, 0.0003784 m, log10 = -3.422, age 0 Ma). The pass-1 GIF is the colorized vane alone (build_frames pass_id=1) and scores cv_sim_similarity 60.3 against the Xosema drake. That is not a specimen match. Image fitness at these subscores is 61.4. Overall 76.5/100 (faithfulness 72.1, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 7f178d2f869f94ba7cd9d9e01aa00da67845de72; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 58, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 7f178d2f869f94ba7cd9d9e01aa00da67845de72, image/png, 545600 B, 1632×984 px, artifact_sha256 c113eb245fd2624c64adf9e5d6e5fec80cb168f07eb96f09fe0b6108d3bb355d (sha256 c113eb245fd2624c64adf9e5d6e5fec80cb168f07eb96f09fe0b6108d3bb355d), spec_fingerprint b47a903373053554b978b71d1931bae7780b1b6bc65d629e52dda1d3d64ccf1f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b47a903373053554b978b71d1931bae7780b1b6bc65d629e52dda1d3d64ccf1f; artifact_sha256: c113eb245fd2624c64adf9e5d6e5fec80cb168f07eb96f09fe0b6108d3bb355d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0/anas_platyrhynchos_drake_specimen.jpg=f1508fedb20fe027..., datasets/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=1111ff8fb8d99074..., datasets/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=d646dccbbd97a151...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the diffusion-driven instability conditions. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Prum & Williamson 2002: within-feather bars, stripes, and spots can be reaction-diffusion patterns. | Inaba & Chuong 2020: macro body pattern and micro within-feather pattern are different levels. | Stavenga et al. 2017: mallard speculum hue is a multilayer, not a pigment wavenumber.; reconstructed_in_script: Near-onset deviation PDE with cubic saturation and an optional quadratic term q U^2. | lambda_star pinned to the campaign anchor 0.0003784 m, not to a published mallard measurement.; transfer_boundary: The Anas chronoseries is 1/1 at 0 Ma. Scale neighbours (348 µm bioelectric, 1.3 mm vertex packing, 2.4 cm plumage block) are other laws or another length, not other chronospecies.; does_not_claim: That 378.4 µm was measured on a mallard feather in the cited papers. | That the green head or the speculum is a Turing pigment. | That the pass-1 vane GIF matches the drake photograph.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'The saved animation must be the specimen-mapped growth, not the vane-only colorization. Pass-1 cv_sim_similarity is 60.3 and image fitness at these subscores is 61.4.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Publish specimen segmentation metrics whose values are not copies of the reference (foreground, coherency, circularity) plus the Du-sweep Pearson r and RMSE.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Show the equal-diffusion control on the same colour scale as the bars so a decayed field is not stretched into a fake pattern, and keep a fixed scale on the growth inset so amplitude actually grows.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.765"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

